    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**1. Fixed governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`):\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- These were previously only available in the default export, but the test imports them as named exports\n- The default export still includes them, so this change is backwards compatible\n\n**2. Fixed toxicity metric function signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`):\n- Changed from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`\n- The issue was that when `runEvaluations` calls metrics as `metric(outs, refs)`, the references array was being bound to `bannedTerms` parameter, causing false toxicity detections\n- Now the references parameter properly accepts the comparison data but is unused, while `bannedTerms` defaults to the correct banned terms list\n\nAll 28 tests now pass, and all existing public exports are preserved.",
